@startuml Pattern_A_Direct
title Pattern A — Direct Point-to-Point (No Middleware, baseline)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

rectangle "CargoWise" as CW {
  component "eAdaptor Next\n(Inbound / Outbound)" as EAN
}
cloud "Client System" as CLIENT

CW --> CLIENT : Outbound XML (HTTP POST)
CLIENT --> CW : Inbound XML (HTTP POST)

note bottom of CW
Client must speak CW's native
XML dialect directly — no
translation layer available.
end note

@enduml

@startuml Pattern_B_PassThrough
title Pattern B — Boomi as Pass-Through Relay

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

rectangle "CargoWise" as CW {
  component "eAdaptor Next" as EAN
}
rectangle "Boomi" as BOOMI {
  component "HTTP Listener" as LISTEN
  component "Forward As-Is\n(protocol translation only)" as FWD
}
cloud "Client System" as CLIENT

CW --> LISTEN : Outbound XML
LISTEN --> FWD
FWD --> CLIENT : Same payload,\ndifferent transport/protocol
CLIENT --> BOOMI : Response
BOOMI --> CW : Ack / status

note bottom of BOOMI
No business logic, no field
mapping — Boomi only bridges
protocol/transport differences
(e.g. HTTPS -> SFTP -> AS2).
end note

@enduml

@startuml Pattern_C_Transform
title Pattern C — Boomi as Transformation / Mapping Layer

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

rectangle "CargoWise" as CW {
  component "eAdaptor Next" as EAN
}
rectangle "Boomi" as BOOMI {
  component "HTTP Listener" as LISTEN
  component "Field Mapping\nCW XML -> Client format" as MAP
  component "Format Conversion\nXML <-> JSON / EDI / flat file" as CONV
  component "Validation" as VAL
}
cloud "Client System" as CLIENT

CW --> LISTEN : Outbound XML (CW schema)
LISTEN --> MAP
MAP --> CONV
CONV --> VAL
VAL --> CLIENT : Client-native format
CLIENT --> BOOMI : Response (client format)
BOOMI --> CW : Mapped ack / status

note bottom of BOOMI
Boomi owns the mapping — CW
and Client schemas never need
to match. Most common pattern
for external client integrations.
end note

@enduml

@startuml Pattern_D_Orchestration
title Pattern D — Boomi as Orchestration Hub (multi-system)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

rectangle "CargoWise" as CW {
  component "eAdaptor Next" as EAN
}
rectangle "Boomi" as BOOMI {
  component "HTTP Listener" as LISTEN
  component "Business Rules Engine" as RULES
  component "Process Orchestration\n(stateful, multi-step)" as ORCH
  component "Retry / Error Queue" as RETRY
  component "Monitoring Dashboard" as MON
}
cloud "Client A" as CLIENTA
rectangle "ERP" as ERP
rectangle "WMS" as WMS

CW --> LISTEN : Outbound XML
LISTEN --> RULES
RULES --> ORCH
ORCH --> CLIENTA : Deliver
ORCH --> ERP : Sync
ORCH --> WMS : Sync
ORCH --> RETRY : On failure
RETRY --> ORCH : Retry per policy
ORCH --> MON : Status / metrics

note bottom of BOOMI
One CW event fans out to N
downstream systems with its
own business logic, retries,
and observability. Highest
capability, highest complexity.
end note

@enduml

@startuml Pattern_E_FileBased
title Pattern E — File / Poll-Based Exchange (decoupled, batch)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

rectangle "CargoWise" as CW {
  component "eAdaptor Next\n(writes file, no live call)" as EAN
}
database "Shared SFTP / AS2\nDrop Location" as SFTP
rectangle "Boomi" as BOOMI {
  component "Scheduled Poller" as POLL
  component "Process on Pickup" as PROC
}
cloud "Client System" as CLIENT

CW --> SFTP : Write XML file\n(scheduled or event-triggered)
POLL --> SFTP : Poll on interval
SFTP --> POLL : New file(s) found
POLL --> PROC
PROC --> CLIENT : Deliver (push or\nclient-side pickup)

note bottom of SFTP
CW and Boomi are never both
online for the exchange to
work — fully decoupled, but
"real-time" only down to the
poll interval.
end note

@enduml

@startuml Pattern_F_DirectDB
title Pattern F — Direct Database Read (bypasses eAdaptor entirely)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

database "CargoWise\nReporting DB (read replica)" as DB
rectangle "Boomi / BI Tool" as BOOMI {
  component "Scheduled SQL Query\nor Reporting Connector" as QUERY
}
cloud "Client / Downstream System" as CLIENT

DB --> QUERY : Read-only, no eAdaptor\nauth/validation/logging layer
QUERY --> CLIENT : Export / sync

note bottom of DB
No business-event trigger, no
schema validation, no message
log or retry semantics — this
is a reporting/BI pattern, not
a transactional integration.
Never write to this DB.
end note

@enduml
